meta {
  name: Extract label from OCR text
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/products/extract-label
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "rawText": "Nutritional information per 100g\nEnergy 1234 kJ / 295 kcal\nFat 12.5 g\nCarbohydrates 30 g\nProtein 8 g\nSalt 0.5 g\nServing size: 30g\nIngredients: oats, sugar, sunflower oil, salt."
  }
}

docs {
  Parses raw OCR text into structured nutritional fields. Requires a registered (non-anonymous) user.

  Text path: send { rawText: string } as JSON. Length must be >= 50 chars (after trimming) and <= 20000 chars (raw).
  Image path: send multipart with image field — pipeline chosen by server VISION_MODE (mock/live/llm).

  Errors: 400 { error: "raw_text_too_short" | "raw_text_too_long" }, 401 (no session), 403 (anonymous session).

  The 20000-char cap bounds how much text the regex parser can be handed — the patterns are linear, and the cap keeps them that way if one ever regresses.
}
